Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• Belts.name: detect titles that contain the string “NXT”.  
• Belts.id / Matches.title_id: link every match to its championship.  
• Matches.duration: find the shortest match length.  
• Matches.title_change: exclude matches in which the belt actually changed hands (value = 1).  
• Matches.winner_id / Matches.loser_id: get the two wrestlers who competed in the chosen match.  
• Wrestlers.id / Wrestlers.name: translate wrestler ids to their names.  

Typical conditions you will need  
• Belts.name LIKE '%NXT%'            – keep only NXT‑branded titles.  
• Matches.title_change = 0           – ignore matches with a title switch.  
• Matches.duration <> ''             – keep matches that have an explicit time.  
• ORDER BY total_seconds ASC LIMIT 1 – pick the shortest one.  


Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that move step‑by‑step from simple inspection to the final answer.  
Feel free to run, inspect, and adjust‑‑they are only SELECTs.

```sql
-- 1) List every belt so we can see if / how “NXT” appears.
SELECT DISTINCT id, name
FROM Belts
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Show only belt names that contain the string “NXT”.
SELECT id, name
FROM Belts
WHERE name LIKE '%NXT%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) All matches that involved an “NXT” belt (any duration, any result).
SELECT m.id AS match_id,
       m.title_id,
       b.name        AS belt_name,
       m.duration,
       m.title_change
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Distinct duration strings we have for those NXT‑title matches.
SELECT DISTINCT m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.duration <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) NXT‑title matches WITHOUT a title switch (title_change = 0).
SELECT m.id,
       m.duration,
       m.title_change
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Same set, but convert duration to total seconds so we can sort numerically.
--    Assumes durations are in the usual "MM:SS" format.
SELECT m.id,
       m.duration,
       (CAST(substr(m.duration, 1, 2) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
        CAST(substr(m.duration, 4, 2) AS INTEGER)) AS total_seconds
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
ORDER BY total_seconds ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Fetch the single shortest NXT title match (still no wrestler names yet).
SELECT m.id,
       m.duration,
       (CAST(substr(m.duration, 1, 2) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
        CAST(substr(m.duration, 4, 2) AS INTEGER)) AS total_seconds
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
ORDER BY total_seconds ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 8) Join wrestler names for that one shortest match to see who won and who lost.
SELECT w1.name AS winner,
       w2.name AS loser,
       m.duration
FROM Matches   AS m
JOIN Belts     AS b  ON b.id = m.title_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS w1 ON w1.id = CAST(m.winner_id AS INTEGER)
JOIN Wrestlers AS w2 ON w2.id = CAST(m.loser_id  AS INTEGER)
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
ORDER BY (CAST(substr(m.duration, 1, 2) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
          CAST(substr(m.duration, 4, 2) AS INTEGER)) ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but restricted to the one shortest match only.
SELECT w1.name AS wrestler_one,
       w2.name AS wrestler_two
FROM Matches   AS m
JOIN Belts     AS b  ON b.id = m.title_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS w1 ON w1.id = CAST(m.winner_id AS INTEGER)
JOIN Wrestlers AS w2 ON w2.id = CAST(m.loser_id  AS INTEGER)
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
ORDER BY (CAST(substr(m.duration, 1, 2) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
          CAST(substr(m.duration, 4, 2) AS INTEGER)) ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final condensed query that directly answers the question:
--     “names of the two wrestlers involved in the shortest NXT title match
--      (with no title change)”.
SELECT w1.name AS wrestler_one,
       w2.name AS wrestler_two
FROM Matches   AS m
JOIN Belts     AS b  ON b.id = m.title_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS w1 ON w1.id = CAST(m.winner_id AS INTEGER)
JOIN Wrestlers AS w2 ON w2.id = CAST(m.loser_id  AS INTEGER)
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
ORDER BY (CAST(substr(m.duration, 1, 2) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
          CAST(substr(m.duration, 4, 2) AS INTEGER)) ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

Running the last query will return exactly the two wrestler names you need.
